WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.800
{Chapter 01}

00:10.200 --> 00:12.490
Really? Where?

00:12.910 --> 00:14.449
Wow, you're right!

00:14.450 --> 00:17.000
Dad, can you stop the car?

00:29.260 --> 00:31.799
Seiha, you have to put on a jacket!

00:31.800 --> 00:33.759
You'll get a fever again.

00:33.760 --> 00:35.470
I'm okay, Mom!

00:36.430 --> 00:38.140
It's so cold!

00:39.060 --> 00:40.600
It's really snow!

00:41.770 --> 00:43.309
Jeez...

00:43.310 --> 00:46.229
Here, Bro! I made a snowball!

00:46.230 --> 00:48.240
Try throwing it, Seiha.

00:49.070 --> 00:51.279
There's a bird on that branch up there.

00:51.280 --> 00:53.200
I think that's a varied tit.

00:56.790 --> 01:00.209
Okay, let's go now. It's getting late.

01:00.210 --> 01:02.249
Seiha, did you aim that throw?

01:02.250 --> 01:02.750
Huh?

01:02.751 --> 01:04.920
Did you aim for the bird?

01:05.800 --> 01:09.299
No, because I didn't want to hit it.

01:09.300 --> 01:11.299
Then did you aim for the branch?

01:11.300 --> 01:12.300
Yep!

01:13.010 --> 01:15.809
I'm glad you weren't the
one who threw the snowball.

01:15.810 --> 01:16.760
Huh?

01:16.761 --> 01:21.310
Because you can hit anything you want.

01:21.730 --> 01:23.269
You could've killed the bird.

01:23.270 --> 01:25.320
Seiha, Takumi! Come on!

01:32.320 --> 01:33.360
Strike!

01:36.370 --> 01:37.660
Okayama Prefecture

01:37.661 --> 01:38.950
Welcome to Nitta

01:56.050 --> 02:01.600
I've heard it said so many times

02:02.310 --> 02:08.520
How it's not going to work out

02:09.480 --> 02:14.990
That nothing will change

02:15.280 --> 02:21.500
Even if I pretended not to listen

02:21.950 --> 02:25.329
I knew it all

02:25.330 --> 02:28.499
I learned this from you

02:28.500 --> 02:36.500
That it's not a failure, even when it is

02:37.890 --> 02:44.479
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

02:44.480 --> 02:51.399
The quiet melodies push me forward

02:51.400 --> 02:57.909
Because the sky is so vast and free

02:57.910 --> 03:05.500
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

03:23.220 --> 03:26.060
Bro, we made it to Grandpa's house!

03:27.520 --> 03:28.520
Okay.

03:29.310 --> 03:31.939
Takumi, good to see you.

03:31.940 --> 03:34.399
Seiha, it's your grandfather.

03:34.400 --> 03:36.950
This is our first time meeting, Seiha.

03:40.070 --> 03:41.579
What's so funny?

03:41.580 --> 03:44.910
You're like the spirit of this plum tree!

03:45.620 --> 03:46.909
A plum spirit?

03:46.910 --> 03:48.960
Well, I'm not exactly
sure how to take that.

03:58.130 --> 04:00.469
How do you like your room?

04:00.470 --> 04:01.759
I'm going to go for a run.

04:01.760 --> 04:03.099
Right now?

04:03.100 --> 04:03.890
Yeah.

04:03.891 --> 04:05.099
Okay.

04:05.100 --> 04:07.980
It might be good for you
to see what's around here.

04:08.270 --> 04:10.520
See that huge building on the hill?

04:11.150 --> 04:12.980
That's Nitta East Junior High.

04:13.440 --> 04:16.569
I know. Their baseball
team isn't that good.

04:16.570 --> 04:17.990
You looked them up?

04:19.030 --> 04:21.739
Is it a problem for you
that they're not good?

04:21.740 --> 04:22.740
No.

04:23.240 --> 04:28.999
But you won't make it to national tournaments
if you're struggling in district tournaments.

04:29.000 --> 04:30.079
We will.

04:30.080 --> 04:36.759
I'd rather have them say we won because I was on
the team instead of it being a foregone conclusion.

04:36.760 --> 04:42.680
I mean, the White Tigers weren't much of a team either,
but we made it to the Chugoku regional tournament.

04:43.510 --> 04:45.970
Although we lost in the semis.

04:54.940 --> 04:56.230
Going out for a jog?

04:58.690 --> 05:01.450
Grandpa, I want to ask you something.

05:02.370 --> 05:05.240
About how to heat a
bath? You need experience.

05:06.200 --> 05:08.250
Can you teach me a breaking ball?

05:09.210 --> 05:10.410
A breaking ball?

05:11.080 --> 05:12.119
Like a curveball?

05:12.120 --> 05:15.130
Yes, and a sinker if possible.

05:15.420 --> 05:18.969
What are you going to do learning
a sinker at twelve or thirteen?

05:18.970 --> 05:21.130
You'll just damage your elbow.

05:21.800 --> 05:26.889
A good pitcher doesn't throw
a half-assed breaking ball.

05:26.890 --> 05:31.769
I can't stand seeing other
pitchers throw pitches that I can't.

05:31.770 --> 05:34.149
What kind of nonsense is that?

05:34.150 --> 05:39.650
It shouldn't matter to you
what other pitchers pitch.

05:40.570 --> 05:42.150
Forget about the reason.

05:42.490 --> 05:45.160
I'm not planning on
using a sinker in a game.

05:46.030 --> 05:48.329
Don't underestimate baseball.

05:48.330 --> 05:50.660
You just want to be able to throw it?

05:51.080 --> 05:52.159
You fool!

05:52.160 --> 05:58.379
Have you thought about how much stress you're going
to be putting on this elbow to learn a sinker?

05:58.380 --> 06:00.670
Instead of learning how to
throw a mediocre sinker now,

06:01.050 --> 06:05.720
just wait until your body develops
enough to pitch it halfway decently.

06:07.100 --> 06:09.930
Now, go on and start your run.

06:10.520 --> 06:12.099
Take a right after the gate.

06:12.100 --> 06:14.440
There's a shrine after
you cross the bridge.

06:14.940 --> 06:17.940
That should be the
perfect distance for a run.

07:05.860 --> 07:07.030
Strike.

07:08.410 --> 07:09.910
Nice form!

07:11.290 --> 07:15.579
I went fishing and a man
came down from the shrine.

07:15.580 --> 07:17.039
I saw it with my own two eyes.

07:17.040 --> 07:19.210
You can fish around here?

07:21.170 --> 07:22.420
They're bluegills.

07:23.920 --> 07:26.049
Hey, Gou. Let's go.

07:26.050 --> 07:28.429
Yeah. It's getting dark.

07:28.430 --> 07:29.760
All right.

07:30.550 --> 07:32.430
Do you want to come
fishing with us next time?

07:32.810 --> 07:34.849
I'm not that interested in fishing.

07:34.850 --> 07:36.980
Are you only interested in baseball?

07:40.110 --> 07:43.480
You're Harada Takumi, aren't you?
From the White Tigers?

07:46.950 --> 07:49.449
Am I really that famous?

07:49.450 --> 07:50.829
I suppose so.

07:50.830 --> 07:54.659
Our team actually made it to the
prefectural tournament last year.

07:54.660 --> 07:55.450
Last year?

07:55.451 --> 08:00.959
Our coach said this pitcher named
Harada is old man Ioka's grandson.

08:00.960 --> 08:04.090
We saw one of your games
from the Chugoku tournament.

08:04.550 --> 08:07.339
You said you made it to the
prefectural tournament last year?

08:07.340 --> 08:09.590
Yeah, with the Nitta Stars.

08:12.560 --> 08:15.390
So are you starting junior high this year?

08:16.680 --> 08:20.270
Obviously! I graduated
grade school just fine.

08:21.110 --> 08:22.899
We'll see you later.

08:22.900 --> 08:24.979
Bye, Gou!

08:24.980 --> 08:25.980
Bye!

08:27.070 --> 08:28.569
You want a ride?

08:28.570 --> 08:30.990
No, I'm good. I'll run.

08:36.910 --> 08:37.660
What's your name?

08:37.660 --> 08:38.660
Huh?

08:38.870 --> 08:41.789
I know it's Gou, but what's your last name?

08:41.790 --> 08:44.049
Oh, it's Nagakura.

08:44.050 --> 08:45.669
I live pretty close to you.

08:45.670 --> 08:50.380
Also, your mom and my
mom went to school together.

08:52.390 --> 08:54.759
I can't wait to see you pitch.

08:54.760 --> 08:56.770
From the batter's box?

08:57.100 --> 09:02.560
I only saw it from a distance, but your pitch didn't
lose any speed by the time it got to the plate.

09:02.980 --> 09:04.110
Of course not.

09:04.570 --> 09:08.990
I bet batters have trouble when
a ball like that comes in low.

09:09.570 --> 09:11.280
If they try to hit it.

09:12.280 --> 09:13.570
And if they don't?

09:14.700 --> 09:15.830
They strike out.

09:21.420 --> 09:22.460
Want me to pitch to you?

09:22.790 --> 09:23.790
Huh?

09:23.960 --> 09:25.419
You're a catcher, right?

09:25.420 --> 09:27.460
Want to catch some of my pitches?

09:31.680 --> 09:33.840
You'll really pitch to me?!

09:35.600 --> 09:36.759
Yeah, sure.

09:36.760 --> 09:39.850
Only if you can catch it, though.

09:41.140 --> 09:43.769
Oh, don't you worry about that.

09:43.770 --> 09:45.860
I'll come by tomorrow morning. That okay?

09:46.320 --> 09:48.609
All our furniture is getting here tomorrow.

09:48.610 --> 09:50.029
I'll be busy in the morning.

09:50.030 --> 09:51.569
I'll help!

09:51.570 --> 09:54.530
I'm pretty strong, so
I know I'll be useful.

09:55.780 --> 09:57.280
Bye! And don't forget!

10:11.090 --> 10:12.379
You were out late.

10:12.380 --> 10:14.299
We started eating without you.

10:14.300 --> 10:17.100
Bro, it's sukiyaki! Hurry up!

10:21.310 --> 10:23.480
You were out for quite a while.

10:23.890 --> 10:26.479
The whole trip should've
barely been five kilometers.

10:26.480 --> 10:29.110
Well, he'd been in a car
for several hours today.

10:29.650 --> 10:31.989
Even Takumi would get exhausted after that.

10:31.990 --> 10:35.069
Do you really believe that, Dad?

10:35.070 --> 10:36.909
Huh? Believe what?

10:36.910 --> 10:40.870
Do you really think I was
late because I got tired?

10:41.540 --> 10:42.620
Is that not the case?

10:44.290 --> 10:46.630
Takumi, what is with your attitude?

10:49.040 --> 10:51.509
Everyone is trying to have a pleasant meal.

10:51.510 --> 10:54.589
You're free to sulk, but
try being more consi...

10:54.590 --> 10:56.259
Makiko, that's enough.

10:56.260 --> 10:58.260
Thank you for watching.

11:03.140 --> 11:05.769
You were talking with
somebody, weren't you?

11:05.770 --> 11:10.770
Right? You met someone along the
way and started talking, didn't you?

11:12.440 --> 11:13.280
Yeah.

11:13.281 --> 11:15.489
I met some weird guy.

11:15.490 --> 11:17.780
His name was Nagakura Gou.

11:18.530 --> 11:22.119
You met Gou? His family
runs Nagakura Hospital.

11:22.120 --> 11:27.119
Makiko, he's the son of your
good friend Ishioka Setsuko.

11:27.120 --> 11:28.120
Oh, that's right!

11:28.380 --> 11:30.749
She had a son the same age as Takumi.

11:30.750 --> 11:31.999
What was he like?

11:32.000 --> 11:33.710
He said he'll come here tomorrow.

11:49.650 --> 11:51.610
Hey, Harada! I've come to help!

11:52.730 --> 11:54.569
Maki, long time no see!

11:54.570 --> 11:55.609
Secchan!

11:55.610 --> 11:57.450
Thank you for coming!

11:57.451 --> 11:59.109
Make sure you put on gloves first.

11:59.110 --> 12:01.199
You don't want to injure your fingers.

12:01.200 --> 12:02.949
I don't need you mothering me.

12:02.950 --> 12:04.700
And don't give me orders.

12:05.620 --> 12:08.120
They say your catcher is like your wife.

12:08.460 --> 12:10.749
I'm just worried about you.

12:10.750 --> 12:12.919
That only applies if
we're in a battery together.

12:12.920 --> 12:15.630
Which we obviously will be!

12:16.420 --> 12:19.680
I don't know if you can
actually catch my pitches.

12:20.140 --> 12:22.639
I know they're fast.

12:22.640 --> 12:23.929
Could you help with this next?

12:23.930 --> 12:24.930
Yeah.

12:25.470 --> 12:30.559
Wait, Harada, you haven't heard
your grandpa's Koshien story?

12:30.560 --> 12:31.650
I'm not interested.

12:33.190 --> 12:36.649
It seems like "I'm not interested"
is your favorite phrase or something.

12:36.650 --> 12:38.859
Are you really not interested in Koshien?

12:38.860 --> 12:39.660
No, I am.

12:39.661 --> 12:42.619
Then why not hear his story?

12:42.620 --> 12:48.079
The only interest I have in
Koshien is to pitch on that mound.

12:48.080 --> 12:51.170
I'm not interested in hearing
about someone who's been there.

12:53.170 --> 12:55.169
You're just like your grandpa.

12:55.170 --> 12:56.589
You both say the same thing.

12:56.590 --> 12:57.629
What do you mean?

12:57.630 --> 13:02.889
One time I begged him to
tell me all about Koshien.

13:02.890 --> 13:08.850
Then he told me to imagine
myself playing baseball there.

13:10.190 --> 13:14.940
And so was little Gou able to picture
himself playing at Koshien Stadium?

13:15.400 --> 13:19.359
Honestly, it didn't really
click with me until recently.

13:19.360 --> 13:21.029
What do you mean, recently?

13:21.030 --> 13:22.700
So you're saying it clicks now?

13:23.030 --> 13:24.529
Oh, for sure!

13:24.530 --> 13:29.200
I saw you pitch at the prefectural
tournament, and then you moved here to Nitta!

13:29.540 --> 13:31.209
And we're going to form a battery!

13:31.210 --> 13:33.960
After I imagined that, it totally clicked!

13:37.800 --> 13:40.840
Thank you so much for your help today.

13:43.640 --> 13:45.970
Wow, so these are bluegills?

13:46.890 --> 13:48.469
Thanks, Gou!

13:48.470 --> 13:49.470
You're welcome.

13:50.560 --> 13:52.479
We're all finished, Harada.

13:52.480 --> 13:54.649
I've been ready for a while now.

13:54.650 --> 13:56.399
Okay, let's do it!

13:56.400 --> 13:57.480
Gou.

13:58.480 --> 13:59.819
We should go.

13:59.820 --> 14:00.610
What?

14:00.611 --> 14:03.489
No way, Mom! This is the
whole reason I came over.

14:03.490 --> 14:05.570
But it's already three o'clock.

14:06.450 --> 14:08.490
You can play together tomorrow.

14:08.910 --> 14:10.829
We're not playing around.

14:10.830 --> 14:13.000
But you don't have time now.

14:13.290 --> 14:15.079
Cram school doesn't start till five.

14:15.080 --> 14:17.169
Don't worry, I'll make it in time.

14:17.170 --> 14:18.170
Gou!

14:19.800 --> 14:21.129
Cram school?

14:21.130 --> 14:23.629
Yep, three days a week.

14:23.630 --> 14:24.889
It sucks.

14:24.890 --> 14:26.640
Don't forget to study.

14:39.570 --> 14:41.190
All right, let's do it.

14:42.280 --> 14:44.110
We'll start easy with a little catch.

14:59.710 --> 15:00.919
You ready?

15:00.920 --> 15:01.840
Yeah.

15:01.840 --> 15:02.840
All right, I'm squatting.

15:11.930 --> 15:13.270
One more!

15:21.690 --> 15:24.279
Are you actually taking this seriously?

15:24.280 --> 15:26.780
I need time to warm up.

15:27.570 --> 15:28.740
I figured as much.

15:29.450 --> 15:32.700
Anybody could throw that pitch.

15:34.790 --> 15:35.500
Seiha!

15:35.500 --> 15:36.500
Huh?!

15:36.710 --> 15:38.289
Go get my cleats!

15:38.290 --> 15:39.290
Okay.

15:43.960 --> 15:49.800
If the pitcher is going to get serious,
then the catcher has to do the same.

15:51.010 --> 15:52.310
Well, well...

15:52.640 --> 15:57.100
I didn't know the catcher had
his own personal equipment.

15:57.810 --> 16:00.650
Must be nice for him to be rich.

16:02.440 --> 16:04.229
Cut it out!

16:04.230 --> 16:07.650
You're the one who said
anybody could throw that last pitch!

16:08.610 --> 16:11.239
Yeah, when you're not pitching seriously!

16:11.240 --> 16:12.950
Am I wrong?!

16:17.290 --> 16:23.000
How does how rich or poor my family
is have anything to do with baseball?

16:25.460 --> 16:27.420
Let's play baseball, Harada.

16:28.180 --> 16:29.300
Fine.

16:31.680 --> 16:32.970
Bro.

16:33.680 --> 16:34.680
All right.

16:34.850 --> 16:37.640
If you throw another weak-ass
pitch like before, I'm gonna clock you!

16:48.110 --> 16:51.030
Follow my signals, Harada!

16:52.200 --> 16:53.200
Signals?

16:53.410 --> 16:55.200
Fastball right down the middle!

17:04.340 --> 17:05.500
Don't drop it.

17:06.000 --> 17:09.509
If there was a runner on first,
he definitely would've stolen second.

17:09.510 --> 17:12.800
Oh, I didn't know you planned
on letting anyone reach base.

17:14.350 --> 17:17.980
Well, there might be one or two every game.

17:40.710 --> 17:42.079
You see that, Harada?!

17:42.080 --> 17:43.329
I caught it!

17:43.330 --> 17:44.789
Looks like it.

17:44.790 --> 17:46.420
Pretty good, huh?

17:47.050 --> 17:48.840
You're a catcher.

17:49.460 --> 17:52.379
Catching pitches is the job description.

17:52.380 --> 17:54.470
It's nothing to brag about.

17:55.430 --> 17:57.350
But it only took five pitches.

17:57.930 --> 18:00.520
I caught it on the fifth pitch.

18:01.600 --> 18:02.850
That's true.

18:04.060 --> 18:06.730
Come on, let's keep this pace up!

18:28.960 --> 18:30.549
You were awesome, Gou!

18:30.550 --> 18:32.720
I wanna play baseball too.

18:34.550 --> 18:36.889
Here, I'll give this to you.

18:36.890 --> 18:38.059
Really?

18:38.060 --> 18:39.060
Yeah.

18:42.230 --> 18:43.270
Thanks!

18:49.570 --> 18:51.109
Seiha.

18:51.110 --> 18:52.110
Yeah?

18:52.740 --> 18:54.069
How did you know?

18:54.070 --> 18:55.070
Huh?

18:57.410 --> 19:02.289
How did you know that I met
someone during my run last night?

19:02.290 --> 19:03.290
I mean,

19:04.040 --> 19:07.080
the only reason you'd
be out so late running

19:07.500 --> 19:11.460
would be either you got hurt or
you were talking to somebody.

19:12.090 --> 19:14.589
You didn't look hurt when you got back,

19:14.590 --> 19:17.339
and you had this happy look on your face.

19:17.340 --> 19:20.680
Wow, you're like a little
Japanese Sherlock Holmes.

19:22.140 --> 19:24.059
I wanna play baseball too.

19:24.060 --> 19:25.600
I'm gonna join a team.

19:26.060 --> 19:28.019
Are you serious about that?

19:28.020 --> 19:29.020
Yeah!

19:29.150 --> 19:32.029
I wanna throw the ball like you do!

19:32.030 --> 19:33.569
You won't be able to.

19:33.570 --> 19:34.110
Huh?

19:34.570 --> 19:37.110
Your body won't be able to keep up.

19:37.490 --> 19:38.280
Mom wouldn't...

19:38.281 --> 19:40.120
Mom's got nothing to do with it!

19:44.080 --> 19:46.870
I wanna beat you.

19:48.920 --> 19:52.630
The ball feels warm in my hands.

20:06.140 --> 20:07.639
Out for a run?

20:07.640 --> 20:08.899
Yeah.

20:08.900 --> 20:10.559
I had a thought yesterday.

20:10.560 --> 20:11.560
Huh?

20:12.020 --> 20:14.149
I think Seiha's fine.

20:14.150 --> 20:15.150
What?

20:15.650 --> 20:17.950
What about Seiha is fine?

20:18.740 --> 20:20.159
His eyes.

20:20.160 --> 20:21.239
His eyes?

20:21.240 --> 20:26.039
His eyes when he was watching
you and Gou play catch were good.

20:26.040 --> 20:28.289
They had a sparkle to them.

20:28.290 --> 20:31.499
Kids with eyes like that get good.

20:31.500 --> 20:33.040
Seiha can't.

20:33.420 --> 20:35.009
He's a frail kid.

20:35.010 --> 20:36.719
There's no way he can play baseball.

20:36.720 --> 20:39.050
Baseball is to be enjoyed.

20:39.590 --> 20:43.009
What's the point of baseball
if you're not having fun?

20:43.010 --> 20:45.809
Just remember Gou's face from yesterday.

20:45.810 --> 20:48.809
He looked like he was having fun, right?

20:48.810 --> 20:50.560
So did Seiha.

20:51.440 --> 20:53.320
They'll get better.

20:55.230 --> 20:57.689
You were watching us?

20:57.690 --> 20:59.320
Yeah, I was.

21:03.620 --> 21:04.830
I'll be back.

21:27.350 --> 21:31.915
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

21:31.916 --> 21:36.479
I saw you running after
a sparkling white ball

21:36.480 --> 21:41.985
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

21:41.986 --> 21:47.490
As it followed a parabola,
disappearing into distant memories

21:50.080 --> 21:54.585
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

21:54.586 --> 21:59.089
You looked back as you
chased after it from afar

21:59.090 --> 22:04.055
The cheers in the stadium echo in my dreams

22:04.056 --> 22:09.019
The cheers in the stadium echo in my dreams

22:09.020 --> 22:13.500
I continue to call out your
name, ever since that fun day

22:13.501 --> 22:17.979
I continue to call out your
name, ever since that fun day

22:17.980 --> 22:19.440
- I love you
- I love you

22:19.443 --> 22:23.175
That was probably the day before eternity

22:23.176 --> 22:26.909
That was probably the day before eternity

22:26.910 --> 22:29.225
If spring comes tomorrow

22:29.226 --> 22:31.539
If spring comes tomorrow

22:31.540 --> 22:33.895
